  <section>
    <h2>Quick Answer</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>The 9th China International Import Expo (CIIE 2026) will be held in Shanghai from November 5–10, 2026, at the National Exhibition and Convention Center (Shanghai).</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      If you are traveling from outside China to attend CIIE, you need to plan two things separately: <strong>your CIIE visitor registration</strong> and <strong>your permission to enter Mainland China</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Depending on your passport and itinerary, you may need a Chinese visa, qualify for a separate visa-free entry policy, or potentially use China's <strong>240-hour visa-free transit policy</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      CIIE attendance itself does not create a special visa exemption. Your China entry eligibility still depends on the immigration rules that apply to your nationality, route, documents, ports and length of stay.
    </p>
  </section>

